ocs**","target":"https://opencode.ai/docs","line":1511},{"title":"contributing docs","target":"/anomalyco/opencode/blob/dev/CONTRIBUTING.md","line":1517},{"title":"Discord","target":"https://discord.gg/opencode","line":1527},{"title":"X.com","target":"https://x.com/opencode","line":1527},{"title":"opencode.ai","target":"https://opencode.ai","line":1533},{"title":"Readme","target":"#readme-ov-file","line":1537},{"title":"MIT license","target":"#MIT-1-ov-file","line":1539},{"title":"Contributing","target":"#contributing-ov-file","line":1543},{"title":"Security policy","target":"#security-ov-file","line":1547},{"title":"Activity","target":"/anomalyco/opencode/activity","line":1549},{"title":"Custom properties","target":"/anomalyco/opencode/custom-properties","line":1551},{"title":"**189.0k** stars","target":"/anomalyco/opencode/stargazers","line":1555},{"title":"**728** watching","target":"/anomalyco/opencode/watchers","line":1559},{"title":"**23.9k** forks","target":"/anomalyco/opencode/forks","line":1563},{"title":"Report repository","target":"/contact/report-content?content_url=https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode&report=anomalyco+(user)","line":1565},{"title":"Terms","target":"https://docs.github.com/site-policy/github-terms/github-terms-of-service","line":1581},{"title":"Privacy","target":"https://docs.github.com/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-privacy-statement","line":1582},{"title":"Security","target":"https://github.com/security","line":1583},{"title":"Status","target":"https://www.githubstatus.com/","line":1584},{"title":"Community","target":"https://github.community/","line":1585},{"title":"Docs","target":"https://docs.github.com/","line":1586},{"title":"Contact","target":"https://support.github.com?tags=dotcom-footer","line":1587},{"title":"\n        \"* Fixed timeline loads that started on assistant replies by backfilling the missing user turn.\\n* Restored typing in the composer while the window is unfocused.\\n* Fixed dropdown search behavior. [(@arvsrn)","target":"https://github.com/arvsrn","line":1668},{"title":"v1.17.13","target":"https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode/releases/tag/v1.17.13","line":1669},{"title":"(@arvsrn)","target":"https://github.com/arvsrn","line":1669},{"title":"(@arvsrn)","target":"https://github.com/arvsrn","line":1669},{"title":"(@arvsrn)","target":"https://github.com/arvsrn","line":1669},{"title":"jazzyalex.github.io/agent-sessions","target":"http://jazzyalex.github.io/agent-sessions","line":1693},{"title":"@0xRango","target":"https://github.com/0xRango","line":1693},{"title":"a8ad74a","target":"https://github.com/sst/opencode/commit/a8ad74aef3f8b6cd84c76855cbbb30f4fb472b86","line":1693},{"title":"opencode session","target":"https://opencode.\\n\\n...\\n\\n> $ cat .opencode/tool/get-current-session-id.ts \\n> import { tool } from \\\"@opencode-ai/plugin\\\"\\n>\\n> export default tool({\\n>   description: \\\"Get the current session ID\\\",\\n>   args: {},\\n>   async execute(args, context","line":1693},{"title":" -n \\\" $session_id \\\" ","target":"-n \\\" $session_id \\\"","line":2576},{"title":"OpenCode","target":"https://opencode.ai","line":2576},{"title":"\n        \"---\\ndescription: Run multiple parallel tasks on the same project without file conflicts.\\ntitle: Workspaces | OpenCode School\\nimage: https://opencode.school/og/lesson/workspaces.png\\n---\\n\\n[ ","target":"https://github.com/opencodeschool/opencode.school","line":2583},{"title":"How to create a workspace","target":"#how-to-create-a-workspace","line":2584},{"title":"The problem workspaces solve","target":"#the-problem-workspaces-solve","line":2584},{"title":"What happens under the hood","target":"#what-happens-under-the-hood","line":2584},{"title":"What workspaces are","target":"#what-workspaces-are","line":2584},{"title":"When to use workspaces","target":"#when-to-use-workspaces","line":2584},{"title":"Git worktrees","target":"https://git-scm.com/docs/git-worktree","line":2584},{"title":"← All lessons","target":"https://opencode.school/","line":2584},{"title":"Enroll for free","target":"https://opencode.school/","line":2584},{"title":"\n        \"> **Built for focused workflows:** browse sessions with a **workspace-aware sidebar** , open each conversation in **dedicated session tabs** , and keep **todos and modified files** visible while you code, whether you work locally or over **Remote SSH** .\\n> \\n> \\n\\nStay in the editor, keep context intact, and manage OpenCode where the code already lives.\\n\\n## Why use it ✨\\n\\n* **Browse sessions by workspace folder** from the Activity Bar\\n* **Open every conversation in its own VS Code tab**\\n* **Track todos and changed files beside the active session**\\n* **Use it in local folders and Remote SSH workspaces**\\n* **Catch missing `opencode` setup early** with built-in environment checks\\n\\nGet the full OpenCode UI workflow inside VS Code\\n\\n## Visual tour 👀\\n\\n### Sessions sidebar\\n\\nThe sidebar gives you a workspace-first view of your OpenCode sessions so you can create, reopen, refresh, and manage conversations without leaving VS Code.\\n\\nBrowse OpenCode sessions by workspace folder from the Activity Bar\\n### Dedicated conversation tabs\\n\\nEach session opens in its own tab, making it easier to keep multiple threads organized while you continue editing code in the same window.\\n\\nOpen each session in a dedicated tab without leaving VS Code\\n\\n### Todos and changed files at a glance\\n\\nCompanion views help you track session-generated tasks and inspect which files changed during the conversation.\\n\\n|Todo view |Modified files |\\n| --- | --- |\\n|Track session todos alongside the active conversation |See which files changed during the session at a glance |\\n\\n## Highlights 🚀\\n\\n* One OpenCode runtime per workspace folder\\n* Session browser with create, open, refresh, and delete actions\\n* A dedicated panel for each workspace-session pair\\n* Todo and modified file companion views\\n* Built-in environment checks with clearer `opencode` setup feedback\\n\\n## Remote SSH ready 🌐\\n\\nOpenCode UI runs on the correct extension host, so Remote SSH sessions stay aligned with the active workspace.\\n* Runs against the remote machine when you use Remote SSH\\n* Preserves workspace identity across local and remote folders\\n* Keeps file opening and panel restore behavior aligned with the active workspace\\n\\n## Requirements\\n\\n* **VS Code `1.94.0` or newer**\\n* **`opencode` installed on the active extension host and available on `PATH`**\\n\\nIf you use Remote SSH, **install `opencode` on the remote host** so the extension can launch `opencode serve` there.\\n\\n## Quick start ⚡\\n\\n1. Open a project folder in VS Code.\\n2. Confirm `opencode` is available in that environment.\\n3. Open the OpenCode view from the Activity Bar.\\n4. Run `OpenCode: Check Environment` if you want to verify setup first.\\n5. Create a new session or reopen one from the sidebar.\\n\\n## Commands\\n\\n* `OpenCode: New Session`\\n* `OpenCode: Refresh`\\n* `OpenCode: Open Session`\\n* `OpenCode: Delete Session`\\n* `OpenCode: Open Output`\\n* `OpenCode: Check Environment`\\n* `OpenCode: Refresh Workspace Sessions`\\n* `OpenCode: Restart Workspace Server`\\n## Notes\\n\\n* **Sessions are organized per workspace folder**\\n* **Remote SSH requires `opencode` on the remote host**\\n* **Environment issues can be checked** with `OpenCode: Check Environment`\\n\\n## Feedback 💬\\n\\nHave an idea or hit a bug? Open an issue at <https://github.com/a710128/opencode-vscode-ui/issues> .\\n\\n### Works with\\n\\nUniversal\\n\\n### Project Details\\n\\n* [a710128/opencode-vscode-ui","target":"https://github.com/a710128/opencode-vscode-ui","line":2599},{"title":"alexgorbatchev/ai-registry-harnesses-opencode-skills/opencode-sessions","target":"https://skillsmp.com/skills/alexgorbatchev-ai-registry-harnesses-opencode-skills-opencode-sessions-skill-md","line":2681}],"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[[40,44],[47,50],[55,59],[62,70],[83,87],[90,101],[106,110],[113,121],[126,130],[133,139],[158,162],[165,167],[202,207],[210,342],[347,351],[354,356],[369,374],[377,501],[503,516],[518,522],[524,528],[530,534],[536,542],[544,552],[554,567],[569,575],[577,583],[585,591],[593,599],[601,618],[620,626],[628,641],[643,649],[651,655],[657,685],[687,703],[705,709],[711,723],[725,737],[739,743],[745,754],[756,766],[768,772],[774,778],[780,790],[792,800],[802,825],[838,843],[846,1592],[1605,1609],[1612,1706],[1772,1777],[1780,2529],[2544,2548],[2551,2645]]},